---
import ContentPage from "../layouts/ContentPage.astro";
import { ORG_EMAIL } from "../lib/seo";

const site = "https://refocus.co.in";
const UPDATED = "2026-09-28";
const mailto = `mailto:${ORG_EMAIL}`;
const title = "Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "How Refocus collects, uses, and shares data in the iOS app, website, and focus sessions — and how to delete your account.";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: "Privacy Policy — Refocus",
    url: `${site}/privacy`,
    description,
    dateModified: new Date(UPDATED).toISOString(),
  },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated={UPDATED}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Refocus ("we", "us") collects, uses, and
    shares information when you use the Refocus iOS app, the website
    (<a href="https://refocus.co.in">refocus.co.in</a>), and the product
    (<a href="https://dashboard.refocus.co.in">dashboard.refocus.co.in</a>).
  </p>

  <p class="contact-lead">
    Questions, or a request about your data? Email
    <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>.
    You can also use <a href="/contact">Contact</a> or
    <a href="/support">Support</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>What we collect depends on how you use Refocus:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account information:</strong> name, email address, username, and
      a user ID. If you create a password, we store it as a secure hash. If you
      use Google or Sign in with Apple, we receive the identifier those
      services share, plus the name and email you allow (Apple may provide a
      private relay address instead of your real email).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Profile photo:</strong> only if you choose one. On iPhone, that
      uses the photo library permission.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Content you create:</strong> messages, community posts, session
      requests, and check-in notes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sessions:</strong> bookings, start and end times, who joined, and
      whether you completed a session. This is product activity tied to your
      account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Camera and microphone:</strong> only while you are in a live
      focus session, so your partner can see and hear you. We do not turn them
      on outside a session. Live video and audio are carried by Daily.co.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Push notifications:</strong> if you allow them, we store a device
      push token so we can send session and account alerts you opted into.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Device and technical data:</strong> device type, operating system,
      app version, and approximate location derived from your IP address, used
      to run and secure the service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Product analytics:</strong> screens you open and actions you take
      in the app and on the website, linked to your account, through PostHog.
      The website also uses cookies and Google Analytics.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create your account and sign you in.</li>
    <li>To match you into focus sessions and run chat, friends, and community.</li>
    <li>To place live video sessions and send the notifications you allow.</li>
    <li>To send account and verification email.</li>
    <li>To understand how the product is used and to fix problems.</li>
    <li>To keep the service secure, moderate abuse, and enforce our <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tracking and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information. We do not use your data to track
    you across other companies' apps or websites for advertising, and the iOS
    app does not use Apple's advertising identifier.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can see your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>People you choose:</strong> session partners, friends, and
      community audiences can see the profile and content you share with them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers,</strong> who process data for us to run
      Refocus:
      <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">MongoDB Atlas</a>
      (database),
      <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Firebase</a>
      and Google Sign-In,
      Apple (Sign in with Apple),
      <a href="https://www.daily.co/legal/privacy/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Daily.co</a>
      (live video),
      <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Resend</a>
      (email),
      <a href="https://ably.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Ably</a>
      (realtime messaging),
      <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Vercel</a>
      and
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Cloudflare</a>
      (hosting),
      <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">PostHog</a>
      (product analytics), and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics</a>
      (website analytics).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal and safety:</strong> if the law requires it, or to protect
      users and the service.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The website uses cookies for authentication and analytics. Because
    <code>refocus.co.in</code> and <code>dashboard.refocus.co.in</code> share
    sign-in, an authentication cookie is scoped to <code>.refocus.co.in</code>.
    You can control cookies in your browser. Blocking some of them can affect
    sign-in.
  </p>

  <h2>Account deletion and retention</h2>
  <p>You can delete your account yourself:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>In the iOS app: Settings → Danger zone → Delete account.</li>
    <li>On the website: Settings → Delete account.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Deletion removes your profile from the product, including friendships and
    your place in sessions. We may keep a limited record — such as the email on
    the account and safety logs — to prevent abuse and meet legal duties. Copies
    can also remain in backups for a limited time.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you cannot open the app, email
    <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a> from the address on the account and ask us
    to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may access, correct, or delete your personal data, and you can export
    it by asking us. Depending on where you live (for example under the EU GDPR
    or India's DPDP Act), you may have additional rights. Email
    <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a> to use them.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Refocus is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
    collect their personal information. If you believe a child has given us
    information, email <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a> and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>International processing</h2>
  <p>
    We and our providers may process information in countries other than yours,
    including the United States and India. We use this data only as described
    in this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The "Last updated" date above will change, and
    when a change is material we will also tell you in the app or by email.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>, or the
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
